  "support": {"syntax": "supported", "compile": "supported", "backend_requirements": [], "replay_fragment": "covered: the A2.7 invariant list over the finite initial and replayed states"},
  "explain": "Each variant is one row of A2.7. The first variant is the reason the check must run even for a zero-action candidate: the goal already holds at W0, and reporting goal_already_holds would validate an impossible state. two_cities_flat declares its flat location set in the profile; the exclusivity check applies only within a declared set. two_cities_undeclared is the same text without the declaration and gets the granularity diagnostic instead of a conflict. The replayed_conflict variant is the only one where the conflict arises after a step; it also pins that a strict text effect and a strict library effect conflicting in the same successor are both preserved and reported. The two accepting variants pin that the check never infers a conflict from absent facts.",
  "notes": "Amended 2026-09-11 (review R4): the flat location set is a profile declaration, not the set of all located_at places with no stated containment."
}
